Rename hotspot's uabs helpers, which C23 took as a library name

glibc 2.41 implements C23, which adds uabs() to <stdlib.h>. hotspot has
carried its own overload set of the same name in globalDefinitions.hpp,
and the int overload now matches the libc declaration exactly, so GCC 14
against this glibc stops with:

  globalDefinitions.hpp: error: 'unsigned int uabs(int)' was declared
  'extern' and later 'static' [-fpermissive]

Upstream OpenJDK fixed mainline the same way: rename the internal
helpers out of the way. hs_uabs here; every call site follows (the
aarch64 and riscv backends use the same helpers, so cross builds for
those targets are covered too).

